Two years ago, my wife and I sat at a kitchen table with a map of Springfield and a question we couldn't shake: *what would it look like for a church to love this whole city?*

Not just the people who already go to church. Not just the neighborhoods that look like us. The whole city — the families on the east side, the students downtown, the retirees who have lived here for fifty years and the young couples who moved here last month.

## A city worth loving

Springfield is full of good people doing good things. But like every city, it's also full of people who are tired, lonely, and quietly wondering if anyone sees them. We believe the local church can be one of the most beautiful answers to that ache.

> "Seek the welfare of the city where I have sent you… and pray to the Lord on its behalf, for in its welfare you will find your welfare." — Jeremiah 29:7

That verse has become something of a banner over Ember Church. We're not here to build a brand. We're here to be a people who seek the good of Springfield.

## What we hope Ember will be

- **A family**, where no one has to walk through life alone.
- **A place to grow**, where honest questions are welcome and Scripture is taught clearly.
- **A people on mission**, serving our neighbors in tangible ways.

## How you can be part of it

Whether you've followed Jesus for decades or you're not sure what you believe, there's a place for you here. Come to a Vision Night, join us on Launch Sunday, or simply reach out — we'd love to buy you a coffee.

We can't wait to see what God does in this city.
